<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#kente-cloth">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kente cloth</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as kente</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kente cloth is a brightly coloured woven textile of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> peoples of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, made from interwoven strips of cloth. It was associated with royalty and important occasions. It is among the internationally recognised cultural legacies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kente-cloth.jpg" alt="Kente cloth" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bottracker · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kent_wove.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
